verdicts.summary:
Judge round 1, water lane: FAIL, lens score 7.4.

The user's main complaints are fixed on their T1 Mac (also checked at T2 and DPR 1.25). I watched every-frame motion sequences (pointer sweeps, corner extremes, hover push-in, real press-and-hold with lunge and release, off-centre hold) against MAIN :5173. The water no longer breaks up, and the front slabs and floes no longer trail sliding dark bands or white tears; MAIN still does. The way-back switches match MAIN within 1 LSB, the merge is clean, typecheck passes, and no page errors appeared.

It fails on two major points:
1. **Not 1:1 with the reference.** At rest, hover and hold the lake is not the reference's, and at rest it is further from it than MAIN:
   - the near water is stripy, about 1.7x the reference's fine texture;
   - the far-right floe reflection columns are the weakest of all sources (lane 21.4 vs F000 34.1);
   - the water under the right front slabs is light and flat (154 vs Cycles 141, F000 100);
   - lake box error vs 5 reference frames is 10.3 (MAIN 8.4);
   - the hold's rolling wave bands are missing.
2. **Frame budget fails while the camera moves.** Frame cost rises 8.6-14.8 % during the pointer sweep, above the 10 % budget, and frames drop in live runs.

There are also minors (a small walk-texel block at a rock waterline during motion; T0 keeps the old fragmenting lake) and one nit (faint speckle when the lake redraws at rest).

